WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.489 --> 00:00:05.159
Nothing is going to bring back the feeling of your first Dark Souls playthrough.

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:10.769
That's the most depressing line I think I've ever started a video with, but it's the truth.

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:16.500
However, I think the remaster could come close, and here's how.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:21.740
So the past few days I've been playing a Dark Souls mod that scatters enemies and items

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:25.820
not in a random manner, but in a calculated, well-designed way.

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:30.840
It's similar to what Scholar of The First Sin did but perhaps even better because

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:36.040
Dark Souls 1 was actually really well designed to begin with. This mod by FT Richter is

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:42.640
This mod by FT Richter is my argument for why the remaster should switch things up

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:48.980
and I think this encounter coming up on screen sums it up best and it's simple

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:52.580
I want that item the Black Knight is guarding

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:55.180
and usually I wouldn't.

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:59.699
Items moving around makes every corner of the world worth exploring again

00:00:59.699 --> 00:01:04.768
and it makes skippable enemies worth fighting and a few minutes later

00:01:04.769 --> 00:01:09.149
I realized that that Black Knight had spotted me on the next balcony and

00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:14.790
had come to ambush me. It went on to make this fight with the Balder Knight unwinnable,

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:17.969
which led to me fleeing towards the blacksmith,

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:20.220
which led to me hoping

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:25.679
they'd fix back steps in the remaster. But, it was a new encounter in an old game

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:28.500
and that's what I want to play for.

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:33.500
Also the Giant Dad is in the forest and so is Oroboro. Those were good memes.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:40.290
Now, there is a huge swath of people who say they don't want any gameplay changed for the remaster

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:42.940
and I can kind of understand that.

00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:49.400
They want the Dark Souls they remember, and they probably want new players to the series to experience

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:52.420
exactly what they did seven years ago.

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:58.880
But to them I say: well, a new experience with items and enemies moved around

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:02.700
ironically is the Dark Souls I remember.

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:04.700
I remember going around corners with my shield up

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:10.960
only to get backstabbed by an enemy that I aggroed behind me. I remember taking stupid risks

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:15.260
for that item over there because it could be something amazing.

00:02:15.269 --> 00:02:18.209
I remember crying out "Where the fuck is the bonfire?!"

00:02:18.519 --> 00:02:24.298
after going through half of Sen's fortress tense because of all the progress I was about to lose.

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:30.000
Those are all things we experienced the first time we played Dark Souls, and those are all the things I

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.310
experienced when I played this mod.

00:02:32.319 --> 00:02:36.500
So, ironically, I think the more they tweak the remaster

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:42.239
the more familiar the experience will be but any item or

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:48.280
enemy randomizer mod can give you those feelings, really. What made this mod, in particular,

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:52.880
special is that the changes have this really good flavor to them.

00:02:53.169 --> 00:02:58.259
It's the little things like this hollow that gets crushed by the dragon when you enter the Burg

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:04.779
Or the bridge then always got bombarded with projectiles now having an item in the middle.

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:08.650
It's being ready to chill during the Moonlight Butterfly fight

00:03:08.650 --> 00:03:14.709
then realizing that they threw a stone Sentinel on the bridge to slow you down if you don't kill it fast enough.

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:19.089
It's dying to the Anor Londo archers and then learning from your mistakes

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:26.470
and dying to the Anor Londo archers and trying to learn from your mistakes, and dying to the Anor Londo archers.

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:31.720
But then getting lucky and making it past the Anor Londo archers. I love it and hate it.

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:32.980
And i love it.

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:38.920
and there's actually a lot you can do from a lore perspective by just putting NPCs in certain locations.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:45.340
For example, there was always two other New Londo sealers mentioned, alongside Ingward.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:49.580
One alongside Lautrec and the other famously had her set

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:55.149
discoverable in Blight Town. Why not make her an NPC at the base of Blight Town?

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:59.560
And, the missing daughter of Chaos now guards the entrance to Quelaag

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:05.200
ingeniously placed between these two egg burdened who you risk aggroing

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:07.820
if you're not careful, during your fight with her.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:11.780
And if there are any items they absolutely should move around,

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:13.560
it's key items and embers.

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:19.929
My search for the large ember brought me all the way down to where the basilisks are, where no

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:23.080
experienced player in their right mind would go again.

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:29.230
And I started to discover all the cut enemies that the creator had put down here like the butcher hollows and

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:33.429
these chaos hollows with the cragspider coming out of their back.

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:37.820
There's just so much room for creativity, and I hope the devs jump at this chance.

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:41.760
The original Dark Souls will always be playable, after all,

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:46.420
but tasteful changes to the remaster could make this amazing.

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:51.960
But all this said, it still lacked that feeling of playing alongside

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:57.400
hundreds and thousands of other people and that's why whether they change a lot, or a little

00:04:57.740 --> 00:05:03.540
in this remaster, the remaster is still gonna feel damn good to play and is worth looking forward to.

